id: pm-c0wthb
title: "Merge fence fails open: an unresolvable pm driver leaves unmarked UU files whose naive resolution silently discards the other branch's fields and history"
description: "pm merge install writes git config merge driver commands that invoke the bare executable name, e.g. merge.pm-item-toon.driver = 'pm merge driver item \"%O\" \"%A\" \"%B\" --item-path item.toon'. Resolution therefore depends entirely on a global pm being on PATH for whatever process runs git merge. When it is not, the fence fails open and loses data silently. Reproduced on a clean two-branch sandbox against dist build 2026.7.25.\n\nControl (pm on PATH): branch agentA sets tag lane-a + priority 1, branch agentB sets tag lane-b + assignee bob on the same item. git merge exits 0 with zero conflicts and produces a correct field-aware union: tags [lane-a, lane-b], priority 1, assignee bob, history unioned to 3 entries. The merge machinery itself is good.\n\nFailure (same merge, PATH without pm): git emits two bare shell lines, 'pm merge driver item ...: line 1: pm: command not found' and the same for the history driver, then reports ordinary 'CONFLICT (content)' for the item .toon and the history .jsonl. Critically the working-tree files contain ZERO conflict markers (grep for '<<<<<<<' returns 0 in both) while git status shows them as UU. The files hold the ours side verbatim: tags [lane-d], assignee dana, 2 history entries. The other branch's fields and its append-only history entry are simply absent from the worktree.\n\nWhy this is a data-loss path rather than a nuisance: the standard resolution reflex, human or agent, is to open a conflicted file, see no markers, conclude it is already resolved, and git add + commit. Doing that commits the ours-only state and permanently drops the other agent's work including its history entries, which is precisely the outcome the append-only history and the field-aware fence exist to prevent. There is no pm-branded diagnostic, no exit-code contract, no post-merge verification hook, and nothing in validate or health that reports 'fence declared in .gitattributes but driver not resolvable'.\n\nExposure is broad, not exotic: CI runners that install pm-cli as a project devDependency, containerized agents, npx-only usage, worktrees or IDE/GUI git clients with a different PATH, and any agent shelling out with a sanitized environment. The documented onboarding step ('each collaborator runs pm merge install once per clone') has no verification that the command it just wrote actually resolves."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: "area:storage",data-loss,merge,multi-agent
created_at: "2026-07-25T21:13:05.285Z"
