author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: "pm merge install verifies that the driver command it writes is resolvable from a clean environment and fails or warns loudly when it is not, recording the resolution strategy it chose. The driver invocation is resilient to a bare pm not being on PATH (absolute path to the resolved binary, a node-based fallback, or an equivalent documented mechanism). When a pm merge driver cannot execute, the merge surfaces a pm-branded diagnostic and does not leave a marker-free UU file that reads as already resolved. pm validate and pm health gain a check that reports a .gitattributes merge fence whose git config driver definitions are missing or unresolvable in the current clone. A regression test performs a two-branch merge with the driver unavailable and asserts no silent ours-wins field or history loss."
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: "Installed merge drivers now pin absolute Node and CLI paths, receive Git's %P item path, persist auditable decisions, and are verified by health/validate plus an adversarial packed-consumer merge."
expected_result: "Clone-local merge drivers remain executable in minimal PATH environments, receive the real Git item path, and fail closed when their installed command configuration drifts."
actual_result: "The installed driver used an unresolved pm command and a literal item-path placeholder, so an unavailable PATH could bypass field-aware merging and no audit surfaced the stale configuration."
